# Everything is excluded, then the build inputs are added back.
#
# Deny-by-default, not a list of things to skip. The Dockerfile's build stage
# does `COPY . .`, and with an allow-list the failure mode of forgetting an entry
# is a build error naming the missing file. With a deny-list it is a secret
# silently baked into an image layer — which is what happened here: with no
# .dockerignore at all, the context was 731MB and included .env (the real
# ENCRYPTION_MASTER_KEY, JWT_SECRET, database password and Proxmox token),
# .dragon-buddy/ and docs/security/. The final stage copies only the binary, but
# layers are extractable: `docker history` and `docker save` both reach them, so
# anything pushed to a registry ships those credentials.
*

# ---- Go: the workspace and all four modules --------------------------------
!go.work
!go.work.sum
!go.mod
!go.sum
!main.go
!cmd/
!internal/
!pkg/
!sdk/go/
!agent/
!tools/

# ---- Frontend --------------------------------------------------------------
# .yarnrc.yml carries `nodeLinker: node-modules`; without it Yarn 4 falls back to
# PnP inside the image and resolves differently from every developer machine.
# package.json carries `packageManager`, which is what corepack reads to pick
# Yarn 4 over the Yarn 1 the node image ships.
!package.json
!yarn.lock
!.yarnrc.yml
!ui/
!sdk/ts/

# ---- Re-excluded even though the paths above allow them ---------------------
# Generated or machine-local, and every one of them either bloats the context or
# would overwrite something the build produces itself.
**/node_modules
**/.yarn
**/dist
internal/api/webdist
bin/
*.test
.git
